  "title": "Bellier et al. 2023 Pink Floyd music listening ECoG: authors' high-frequency activity (HFA, 70-150 Hz) for 29 patients",
  "description": "This dataset is a BIDS-formatted derivative of the preprocessed electrocorticography (ECoG) data from Bellier et al. (2023). It contains high-frequency activity (HFA, 70-150 Hz) envelopes at 100 Hz for 29 patients with pharmacoresistant epilepsy who passively listened to Pink Floyd's 'Another Brick in the Wall, Part 1'. Electrode coordinates in MNI space, the authors' bad-channel flags, and outlier annotations are included. The raw ECoG recordings and the stimulus audio are not redistributed.",
  "methods_description": "ECoG was recorded at 1200 Hz with g.USBamp amplifiers and BCI2000 at Albany Medical Center using Ad-Tech platinum-iridium grids and strips. HFA was computed by notch filtering, 1 Hz high-pass filtering, and band-passing into 20-Hz sub-bands between 70 and 150 Hz. A median common average reference was applied per sub-band, followed by the Hilbert envelope and robust scaling. The sub-bands were averaged, the result was downsampled to 100 Hz, and samples above 7 SD were flagged as outliers.",
  "license": "CC-BY-4.0",
